{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The realtime socket's frames and the ICE server list, as the Worker sends and takes them: docs/API.md (Realtime: GET /v1/realtime; ICE servers: GET /v1/ice-servers). This is the Worker's own JSON, snake_case, around what the devices seal for each other: a `sealed` value here is a real one, made as sealed-v1.json says, and wire-v1.json has what may be inside.",
    "`frames_from_server`: text frames an app receives. `apps` says what an app makes of `json`: \"takes\" (it reads), or \"drops\" (it fails to read, and the frame is dropped as if it never came). `reads` is what it reads, with each `sealed` value opened by `signer` as device `as`, at the time `now`: a status as its camera's (null where it doesn't open so), a signal's payload as sent by `from` for `session`. `plan_refusal` is the code where it is one of the home's plan's (docs/API.md, Plans), else null.",
    "`frames_to_server`: text frames an app sends, here as device `as`. `worker` says what the Worker makes of each: \"takes\", and then `delivers` is the frame the device it's for receives; or \"drops\", without an answer (docs/API.md: a frame the server drops is never answered).",
    "`ice_servers`: answers to GET /v1/ice-servers. `apps` is \"takes\" or \"refuses\" (the answer fails to read, and the app goes on with STUN alone); `reads` gives each server with null for what it lacks.",
    "`heartbeat`: the text frame an app sends and the one the Worker answers with, neither of them JSON, and how often docs/API.md asks for one.",
    "JSON is read as values: key order and how a number is written (1 or 1.0) don't matter, but a number is never text and true is never 1.",
    "Made by server/scripts/vectors.mjs from fixed keys that were made up for these files; nothing here was ever a real home's. No vector is ever removed: a format the apps stop opening stays, as one that must fail. Read by SharedTests/RealtimeVectorTests.swift (what the Apple apps' own types read: a presence frame's devices, what's sealed inside, the plan's codes, the ICE server list, the heartbeat; `SignalingClient`'s reading of a whole frame is private to it), server/test/vectors.test.ts (the Worker itself: what it takes, drops, delivers and sends) and android/core's RealtimeVectorTest."
  ],
